WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.025
Lab 2 runs the guide's validate queries
in a test tenant, never production.

2
00:00:05.025 --> 00:00:08.025
The authors haven't run
them, as the page says.

3
00:00:08.025 --> 00:00:11.150
Every step reads; nothing
in the tenant changes.

4
00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:15.508
You need Module 1's test tenant and
reader account, with vulnerability data

5
00:00:15.508 --> 00:00:19.725
from at least one onboarded device,
and at least one incident in the queue.

6
00:00:19.725 --> 00:00:22.437
Module 1's detection test raises one.

7
00:00:22.437 --> 00:00:24.863
Step one connects in the tenant's cloud.

8
00:00:24.863 --> 00:00:28.460
Step two files the high and
critical vulnerabilities,

9
00:00:28.460 --> 00:00:31.338
by vendor, software
and recommended update.

10
00:00:31.338 --> 00:00:35.526
One caution the guide records: Learn's
table reference doesn't list the

11
00:00:35.526 --> 00:00:40.149
severity strings, so the guide uses
critical and high as the portal shows them.

12
00:00:40.149 --> 00:00:44.562
If the file comes back empty, check the
values in your tenant before you trust it.

13
00:00:44.562 --> 00:00:48.934
Step three files the exposed and
internet-facing Windows devices,

14
00:00:48.934 --> 00:00:51.637
with their asset value and machine group.

15
00:00:51.637 --> 00:00:54.366
The guide's pass: every
row has an owner in the

16
00:00:54.366 --> 00:00:57.840
decision record and a ticket
in the remediation queue.
